  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nPutting the `align` attribute on an img element behaves similar to `float`. Not sure what exact values are allowed, but `<img align=\"left\">` is a left-floating image in Chromium, WebKit and Firefox. (\"right\" also works)\n\nThe spec only describes \"center\" and \"middle\", saying they should vertically center the element. (https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attributes-for-embedded-content-and-images)",
